Part 7: Storage & Quotas - Managing Your Data
Q23: How much backup storage do we get? What happens if we run out?
A: Your storage quota depends on your subscription plan.
Plan	Storage	What it means
Trial	10 GB	Enough for ~1,000 users' data
Basic	100 GB	Enough for ~10,000 users
Professional	500 GB	Enough for ~50,000 users
Enterprise	Custom	As much as you need
What happens when you approach the limit:
•	80% used - Warning notification (yellow alert)
•	95% used - Critical warning (red alert)
•	100% used - New backups will fail until space is freed
What to do if you're running out:
•	Option 1: Reduce retention period (keep fewer old backups)
•	Option 2: Delete old backups manually
•	Option 3: Upgrade your plan for more storage
•	Option 4: Archive old backups to cheaper storage (Glacier)
Proactive management: The system shows your current usage on the dashboard. Check it monthly to avoid surprises.
Q24: Can we archive old backups to cheaper storage?
A: Yes! This is called tiered storage or lifecycle management.
Storage tiers (from most expensive to least):
•	Standard - Fast access, good for recent backups
•	Intelligent - Automatically moves cold data to cheaper tiers
•	Glacier - Cheaper, but takes hours to retrieve
•	Deep Archive - Cheapest, but takes 12+ hours to retrieve
Automatic archiving rules:
•	Backups older than 30 days → Move to Intelligent tier
•	Backups older than 90 days → Move to Glacier
•	Backups older than 365 days → Move to Deep Archive
What this means for you: You pay less for old backups you probably won't need. If you do need them, you can still retrieve them - it just takes longer (hours instead of minutes).
Example: A backup from 11 months ago costs pennies to store, but you can still restore it if needed for an audit. It just might take 12 hours to become available.
